# reconciliation-investigator — .gitignore (Ares V2 python-strands profile)
#
# *.log keeps agent-memory/guard-audit.log runtime-only (the project
# convention; aresV2 itself tracks its own log deliberately — projects
# do not).

*.log

# environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code local state
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Eval report artifact — regenerated by every verify.sh step-6 run
# (experiment.to_file + report.to_file outputs); capture a copy into
# agent-memory/evidence/ when a run's numbers matter, do not commit the
# working copy.
*_evaluation.json
*_report.json

# Runtime stores (EVAL_MODE=1): drafts, tickets, correction overrides,
# audit log, consumed tokens — application state, not source.
runtime/

# Sensitive planning documents (defense-in-depth ONLY — the real files
# live outside the repository tree; see
# docs/SENSITIVE-PLANNING-DOCS-RELOCATED.md). These patterns exist so
# an accidentally recreated file of these classes cannot be staged by a
# blanket `git add -A`; a deliberately tokenized document that must be
# tracked despite matching needs `git add -f`. The globs are
# prefix-OPTIONAL on purpose: the real relocated names are mixed — the
# privacy-audit and rewrite-plan docs carry a leading project-area
# prefix, the backup-chain doc carries none (which the earlier
# '*-backup-chain-...' form never matched — fixed 2026-09-06).
docs/*privacy-audit-*.md
docs/*rewrite-execution-plan-*.md
docs/*backup-chain-investigation-*.md
agent-memory/*privacy-audit-*.md
agent-memory/*rewrite-execution-plan-*.md
agent-memory/*backup-chain-investigation-*.md
